# Revised Implementation Plan — Jira-to-Regression VS Code Agent (v2)

This plan supersedes the first one. Every correction from my re-verification is baked in rather than bolted on: the repository is never swapped out from under the chat session, Git is never allowed to destroy work implicitly, execution commands come from a committed per-repo config instead of guesswork, credentials never touch the chat or the model, browser automation is per-runner and fails into a manual handoff, the report is not pushed onto a verified commit, and failures are classified rather than always rewinding to planning.

Verified against the current API surface: `vscode.chat.createChatParticipant`, `ChatRequest.model` (the user's selected model), `ChatResponseStream.markdown/progress/button/anchor/filetree`, `ChatParticipant.followupProvider`, `lm.registerTool`/`lm.invokeTool`, `ExtensionContext.secrets`, `workspace.updateWorkspaceFolders`. Sources: [Chat Participant API](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/ai/chat), [Language Model API](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/ai/language-model), [VS Code API reference](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/references/vscode-api).

---

## 1. Product shape

One chat participant, `@jira-flow`, that runs a **persisted, resumable, deterministic state machine** with named human checkpoints. The agent orchestrates the steps itself (this is why a participant, not a tool, is the entry point — participants own the orchestration, tools are invoked by someone else's orchestrator).

Two hard invariants that drive most of the design:

1. **The session outlives any single chat turn.** The user will be away for minutes or hours at the deploy and test-runner checkpoints. State lives on disk; every turn re-reads it.
2. **The agent's working directory is a variable, not the workspace.** All Git, build, run, and file operations take an explicit `cwd`. The VS Code window is never reloaded as part of the happy path, so the chat session is never lost.

### 1.1 Flow (revised)

```
@jira-flow hi
 ├─ S1  COLLECT_TICKET          ask Jira key / description / acceptance criteria
 ├─ S2  COLLECT_REPO            ask absolute repo path → validate → set session.cwd
 ├─ S3  LOAD_EXEC_CONFIG        read .vscode/jira-flow.yml, or generate+confirm one
 ├─ S4  COLLECT_GIT_STRATEGY    base branch, feature branch, commit message
 ├─ S5  PRECHECK_WORKTREE       dirty tree → abort / stash / (explicit) discard
 ├─ S6  SYNC_AND_BRANCH         fetch → switch base → reset --hard → switch -c feature
 ├─ S7  ANALYZE                 index whole repo, deep-read relevant files
 ├─ S8  PLAN                    AC-traceable plan, rendered + written to disk
 ├─ S9  AWAIT_PLAN_APPROVAL     ⏸ human: approve / request changes
 ├─ S10 IMPLEMENT               bounded tool-calling edit loop
 ├─ S11 REVIEW_DIFF             ⏸ human (configurable): show diff, accept / revise
 ├─ S12 BUILD                   configured clean build + tests, bounded fix loop
 ├─ S13 RUN_AND_VERIFY          start app w/ configured dev env → configured health URL → stop
 ├─ S14 COMMIT_AND_PUSH         commit + push feature branch
 ├─ S15 AWAIT_DEV_DEPLOY        ⏸ human: deploy to dev, reply done
 ├─ S16 AWAIT_RUNNER_URL        ⏸ human: start test runner locally, send URL
 ├─ S17 COLLECT_CREDENTIALS     ⏸ human: secure inputs (kID/password, clientId/secret)
 ├─ S18 REGRESSION              profile-driven Playwright run, manual-handoff on miss
 ├─ S19 COLLECT_RESULTS         download + parse + screenshot
 ├─ S20 AWAIT_TEST_VERDICT      ⏸ human: pass / fail
 ├─ S21 REPORT                  ask format → write md/docx as artifact (not auto-pushed)
 ├─ S22 AWAIT_LOG_VALIDATION    ⏸ human: validate logs
 └─ S23 CLOSE                   wipe secrets, archive session

 Any error → S_TRIAGE (classify) → retry / re-ask / fix-loop / replan / pause
```

`⏸` marks the eleven points where the machine stops and waits. Everything else runs to completion and auto-advances within the same turn.

