## 2. Architecture

### 2.1 Layers

| Layer | Responsibility | Never does |
|---|---|---|
| `chat/` | Participant handler, intent parsing, rendering, followups | Business logic, process spawning |
| `workflow/` | State machine, persistence, resume, failure triage | Direct I/O |
| `stages/` | One file per state: `onEnter`, `onUserMessage` | Own its own persistence |
| `services/` | git, exec, config, index, llm, browser, secrets, report | Know about chat |
| `util/` | logger, redactor, tokens, retry, paths | — |

The stage layer is the only place that knows the order of operations; services are all independently testable with a temp repo and no VS Code host.

