### 2.3 Model access

Use `request.model` — the model the user picked in the chat dropdown. Only fall back to `lm.selectChatModels({ vendor: 'copilot' })` when a background stage needs a model outside a live request (there are none in this design; all stages run inside a turn). No hardcoded model family. No `extensionDependencies` on Copilot unless the extension has no non-chat surface.

```ts
const llm = new Llm(request.model, { redact, logger, token });
const plan = await llm.json(PlanSchema, plannerPrompt, contextMessages);
```

`Llm` provides three primitives: `text()`, `json(schema, ...)` with one reprompt on schema failure, and `toolLoop({ tools, maxIterations, onProgress })`.

### 2.4 Persistence and resume

```ts
// store.ts
// Primary:   <repo>/.jira-flow/session.json      (portable, survives window changes)
// Index:     globalState['jiraFlow.activeSessions'] = [{ id, repoPath, state, updatedAt }]
```

- Written **before and after** every automated stage, so a crash lands on a known state.
- `.jira-flow/` is added to `.git/info/exclude`, never to the repo's `.gitignore`.
- On activation, if an active non-terminal session exists, show a status-bar item `$(rocket) jira-flow: S12 BUILD` and one notification with a **Resume** button that runs `workbench.action.chat.open` with `query: '@jira-flow /resume'`. No auto-injected assistant turns.

