## 6. Git: safe by construction (correction 1)

### 6.1 `s05_precheckWorktree.ts`

```bash
git -C <cwd> rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD        # recorded
git -C <cwd> rev-parse HEAD                     # headShaAtStart, always logged
git -C <cwd> status --porcelain --untracked-files=all
```

If output is non-empty, the machine **stops and asks**, showing the file list:

- `[Stash]` → `git stash push --include-untracked -m "jira-flow/<key>/<iso>"`; store `stashRef`; report it in the final summary and on abort.
- `[Abort]` (default) → stay in S5, tell the user to handle it.
- `[Discard]` → requires the user to type the exact phrase `discard my changes`; only then `git reset --hard && git clean -fd`. Never triggered by a bare "yes".

Also verified here: no in-progress rebase/merge/cherry-pick (`.git/REBASE_HEAD`, `MERGE_HEAD`), no detached HEAD surprise, and `git rev-parse --is-shallow-repository` (shallow clones break `reset --hard origin/<base>` history assumptions — warn).

### 6.2 `s06_syncAndBranch.ts`

```bash
git -C <cwd> fetch origin --prune --tags
git -C <cwd> rev-parse --verify origin/<base>        # else: list candidates, back to S4
git -C <cwd> switch <base>                           # or: switch -c <base> --track origin/<base>
git -C <cwd> reset --hard origin/<base>              # "force pull", explicit and scoped
git -C <cwd> rev-parse HEAD                          # baseSha
git -C <cwd> check-ref-format --branch <feature>
git -C <cwd> switch -c <feature>                     # if exists: [Reuse] [Rename] [Delete & recreate]
```

Notes on what changed from v1:

- No bare `git pull` on an arbitrary current branch. The first network op is `fetch`, which mutates no working tree.
- `reset --hard` is applied **only after** `switch <base>` succeeded and only against `origin/<base>`, and only after S5 cleared or stashed the tree.
- `switch` instead of `checkout` throughout — it refuses ambiguous path/branch arguments.
- Rerun-safe: if the feature branch already exists at `baseSha`, S6 is a no-op, so triage can re-enter it freely.

### 6.3 `services/git.ts`

Thin wrapper over the `git` binary via `exec.ts`, not a library that hides raw commands. Every call logs `cwd`, argv, exit code, duration, and the first/last 40 lines of output. Two helper predicates used by triage: `isTransientGitError(stderr)` (DNS, connection reset, 5xx, `could not read Username` → auth, which is *not* transient) and `isConflictError(stderr)`.

