## 11. Reporting without poisoning the verified commit (correction 9)

The report is produced after deploy and regression, so committing it to the feature branch would put an untested commit on top of the SHA that was actually verified. Default behaviour therefore:

- Write artifacts to `exec.report.outputDir` (git-excluded): `<KEY>-report.md` and/or `.docx`, plus results files and screenshots.
- `commitToBranch: false` by default. Offer `[Save as artifact] [Attach to Jira] [Commit as docs-only commit]`; the third option commits with message `docs(<KEY>): implementation report [no functional change]` and the report itself states that this commit was added **after** verification and contains no source changes.
- If documentation is a deliverable of the ticket, the plan must include it as a step, the doc is written during S10, and it is covered by the same build/verify/push cycle — no post-hoc exception.

Report contents (all redacted): ticket + AC with per-AC step mapping and coverage warnings; repo/remote/base SHA/feature branch/pushed SHA/PR link; final plan + revision history and rejection feedback; files changed with `git diff --stat baseSha..pushedSha`; build command, attempts, duration, log link, fix-loop summary; runtime verification (exact URL, status, body, timestamp); deploy confirmation and note; regression (runner URL, profile + version, validated or step-confirm, counts, result file paths, embedded screenshots, **manual steps performed by the human**); full incident log with classifications and actions; appendix of every command with cwd, exit code, duration.

`s22_awaitLogValidation.ts` gives `[Agent log] [Build log] [App log] [Artifacts folder]` and accepts `validated` or `issue: …`. `s23_close.ts` wipes secrets, reports any outstanding `stashRef`, archives the session to `.jira-flow/sessions/<id>.json`, clears the active index, and prints the final summary.

